From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Subject: RK3576 in rocket, and how you would want 102 commits submitted

Hi Tomeu,

RK3576 runs MobileNet V1 end to end on rocket now and every shape in my
regression set comes back correct or within one count. I have 102 commits on
top of 25.3.0 to get there and none of them are upstream, so I would rather ask
how you want them submitted than reshape them the wrong way.

  mn_conv0, the first convolution      32 of 32 channels
  conv2d-cal                           128 of 128
  pointwise, 33 in 64 out              64 of 64
  pointwise, 64 in 41 out              41 of 41
  pointwise, 64 in 56 out              56 of 56
  mobilenet_v1_1.0_224_quant           1000 of 1001, worst channel off by 4

The 102 are RK3576 specific throughout. The register layout differs from the
RK3588 map at shared offsets, the first convolution takes its own datapath, and
the PC dispatch needed a different task field layout, so they are not a thin
layer over what is there.

One of them might matter to RK3588 and I cannot tell from here. rkt_regcmd.c
picks DPU 0x4050 with

    (oc % 32) == 0 ? 0x80011111 : 0x80011011

I fitted that on ten vendor models compiled at 16 to 160 output channels in
steps of 16, ten out of ten. Every one of those counts is a multiple of 16, and
on that set oc % 32 == 0 and DIV_ROUND_UP(oc, 16) being even are the same
predicate, so the sweep could not tell them apart. They part company only where
a count is a multiple of neither, and 56 is one. With the modulo form that
layer times out on RK3576 and with the parity form it is 56 of 56 correct.

Igor Paunovic has since run MobileNet on RK3588 with upstream Mesa and got
1001 of 1001 within one count without this change, but 1001 is not a
discriminating count either, DIV_ROUND_UP(1001,16) being odd. If anyone has an
RK3588 to hand, an output channel count of 56, 88 or 120 is where the two forms
disagree.

Two things I would like to know. Would you rather have one series covering
RK3576, or a minimal enablement first with depthwise and the rest following.
And is anyone else already working on RK3576 in rocket, so that I do not
duplicate them.

Jiaxing
